<workflow name="process-captures">
  <description>
    Process capture sessions through intake: transcribe audio, establish purpose,
    describe images, assemble timeline, and rename.
  </description>

  <step id="transcribe">
    <description>Transcribe all audio clips with word-level timestamps</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell>
        found=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          for card in "$dir"*.audio.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="new"' "$card"; then
              found=$((found + 1))
            fi
          done
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found audio clip(s) to transcribe"
      </shell>
      <why>No untranscribed audio clips in capture sessions</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <shell>cb transcribe-captures</shell>
    </run>

    <validate severity="warn">
      <shell>
        remaining=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          for card in "$dir"*.audio.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="new"' "$card"; then
              remaining=$((remaining + 1))
            fi
          done
        done
        echo "Untranscribed audio remaining: $remaining"
        [ "$remaining" -eq 0 ]
      </shell>
      <instruction>All audio cards should have status="transcribed" after this step.</instruction>
      <why>Later steps depend on all audio being transcribed with timing data.</why>
    </validate>
  </step>

  <step id="summarize">
    <description>Write one-sentence summaries for each audio clip</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell pass-output="true">
        found=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          for card in "$dir"*.audio.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="transcribed"' "$card" &amp;&amp; grep -q '&lt;summary/&gt;\|&lt;summary&gt;&lt;/summary&gt;' "$card"; then
              echo "  Needs summary: $card"
              found=$((found + 1))
            fi
          done
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found audio clip(s) needing summaries"
      </shell>
      <why>No audio clips need summaries</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="haiku" max-turns="10">
        You are summarizing audio transcripts in capture sessions.

        YOUR TASK:
        For each audio card listed in the precheck output, read it and write a one-sentence summary
        focused on what the user is trying to do or communicate. The summary should help a future
        agent understand the purpose and content of this audio clip.

        STEP 1 - READ ALL AUDIO CARDS:
        Read each audio card listed above. They contain &lt;transcript&gt; elements with the transcribed text.

        STEP 2 - WRITE SUMMARIES:
        For each card, edit it to fill in the &lt;summary&gt; element with one sentence.
        Focus on user intent: what are they trying to accomplish, explain, or capture?

        COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Summarize audio clips

        Triggered-By: cb workflow
        Phase: summarize
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>
  </step>

  <step id="purpose">
    <description>Establish the purpose of each capture session from audio summaries</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell pass-output="true">
        found=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          session=$(ls "$dir"*.capture-session.card 2>/dev/null | head -1)
          [ -f "$session" ] || continue
          # Skip if already has purpose with text content
          if grep -qE '&lt;purpose&gt;.+&lt;/purpose&gt;' "$session"; then
            continue
          fi
          # Check if there are audio clips with summaries (non-empty summary)
          has_summaries=0
          for card in "$dir"*.audio.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="transcribed"' "$card" &amp;&amp; ! grep -q '&lt;summary/&gt;' "$card" &amp;&amp; grep -qE '&lt;summary&gt;.+&lt;/summary&gt;' "$card"; then
              has_summaries=1
              break
            fi
          done
          if [ "$has_summaries" -eq 1 ]; then
            echo "  Needs purpose: $session"
            found=$((found + 1))
          fi
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found session(s) needing purpose"
      </shell>
      <why>No sessions need purpose established</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="opus" max-turns="10">
        You are establishing the purpose of capture sessions.

        YOUR TASK:
        For each session card listed in the precheck output, synthesize the audio summaries
        into a single &lt;purpose&gt; statement on the session card.

        STEP 1 - READ CONTEXT:
        For each session listed above:
        1. Read the session card
        2. Read all audio cards in the same directory (they have &lt;summary&gt; elements)

        STEP 2 - WRITE PURPOSE:
        The &lt;purpose&gt; element should be one sentence answering: "What is the user trying to do?"
        This isn't a summary of what was said — it's an interpretation of the user's intent.

        Examples:
        - "User is documenting a whiteboard brainstorm about Q2 product roadmap"
        - "User is capturing notes from a meeting about the API redesign"
        - "User is recording observations while testing the new checkout flow"

        Edit the session card to fill in the &lt;purpose&gt; element.

        COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Establish session purposes

        Triggered-By: cb workflow
        Phase: purpose
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>
  </step>

  <step id="describe-images">
    <description>Describe and rename all images across capture sessions</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell pass-output="true">
        found=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          session=$(ls "$dir"*.capture-session.card 2>/dev/null | head -1)
          purpose=""
          if [ -f "$session" ]; then
            purpose=$(sed -n 's/.*&lt;purpose&gt;\(.*\)&lt;\/purpose&gt;.*/\1/p' "$session" 2>/dev/null || true)
          fi
          for card in "$dir"*.image.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="new"' "$card"; then
              echo "  Image: $card"
              found=$((found + 1))
            fi
          done
          if [ -n "$purpose" ] &amp;&amp; [ "$found" -gt 0 ]; then
            echo "  Session purpose: $purpose"
          fi
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found image(s) to describe"
      </shell>
      <why>No images need description</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="haiku" max-turns="35">
        You are describing and organizing images from capture sessions.

        YOUR TASK:
        Process ALL images listed in the precheck output. For each image:
        1. View the attached image file (same basename, e.g. photo-001.jpg for photo-001.image.card)
        2. Write a one-sentence &lt;description&gt; — oriented toward telling a future agent what's useful
        3. If the image contains readable text:
           - Set has-text="true" on the &lt;image&gt; element
           - Create &lt;text source="..."&gt; elements with the transcribed content in Markdown
           - The source attribute describes what the text is on (e.g. "whiteboard", "business card", "screen")
           - Multiple &lt;text&gt; elements are allowed for different text sources
        4. If no text: set has-text="false"
        5. Rename via cb move to photo-NNN-short-name.image.card (keep the NNN prefix, add a descriptive slug)
        6. Set status="analyzed" (or "invalid" for accidental/useless captures)

        Use the session purpose (shown above) to inform your descriptions — focus on what's relevant
        to the user's goal.

        RENAMING:
        ```
        cb move box/inbox/capture-.../photo-000.image.card box/inbox/capture-.../photo-000-whiteboard.image.card
        ```

        IMPORTANT: Process ALL images before committing. Do not commit after each image.

        COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Describe images: &lt;N&gt; analyzed, &lt;M&gt; invalid

        Triggered-By: cb workflow
        Phase: describe-images
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>

    <validate severity="warn">
      <shell>
        remaining=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          for card in "$dir"*.image.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="new"' "$card"; then
              remaining=$((remaining + 1))
            fi
          done
        done
        echo "Unprocessed images remaining: $remaining"
        [ "$remaining" -eq 0 ]
      </shell>
      <instruction>All image cards should have status="analyzed" or "invalid".</instruction>
      <why>The timeline assembly step needs all images processed.</why>
    </validate>
  </step>

  <step id="assemble">
    <description>Assemble structured timeline from timing data and images</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell>
        found=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          session=$(ls "$dir"*.capture-session.card 2>/dev/null | head -1)
          [ -f "$session" ] || continue
          # Check all audio transcribed
          audio_ready=1
          for card in "$dir"*.audio.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if ! grep -q 'status="transcribed"' "$card"; then
              audio_ready=0
              break
            fi
          done
          # Check all images analyzed/invalid
          images_ready=1
          for card in "$dir"*.image.card; do
            [ -f "$card" ] || continue
            if grep -q 'status="new"' "$card"; then
              images_ready=0
              break
            fi
          done
          if [ "$audio_ready" -eq 1 ] &amp;&amp; [ "$images_ready" -eq 1 ]; then
            # Check transcript not already assembled (has children)
            if grep -q '&lt;transcript/&gt;\|&lt;transcript&gt;&lt;/transcript&gt;' "$session"; then
              found=$((found + 1))
            fi
          fi
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found session(s) ready for timeline assembly"
      </shell>
      <why>No sessions are ready for assembly (need all audio transcribed and all images analyzed)</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <shell>cb assemble-timeline</shell>
    </run>
  </step>

  <step id="rename">
    <description>Rename session directories to descriptive names</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell pass-output="true">
        found=0
        for dir in box/inbox/capture-*/; do
          [ -d "$dir" ] || continue
          session=$(ls "$dir"*.capture-session.card 2>/dev/null | head -1)
          [ -f "$session" ] || continue
          # Has purpose with text content
          has_purpose=0
          if grep -qE '&lt;purpose&gt;.+&lt;/purpose&gt;' "$session"; then
            has_purpose=1
          fi
          # Check transcript has children (not empty)
          has_transcript=0
          if grep -q '&lt;text&gt;\|&lt;silence \|&lt;image ' "$session"; then
            has_transcript=1
          fi
          status=$(grep -oE 'status="[^"]*"' "$session" | head -1 | grep -oE '"[^"]*"' | tr -d '"')
          if [ "$has_purpose" -eq 1 ] &amp;&amp; [ "$has_transcript" -eq 1 ] &amp;&amp; [ "$status" != "intake-complete" ]; then
            echo "  Ready: $dir"
            echo "  Session: $session"
            found=$((found + 1))
          fi
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found session(s) to rename"
      </shell>
      <why>No sessions are ready for renaming</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="haiku" max-turns="20">
        You are renaming capture session directories to descriptive names.

        YOUR TASK:
        For each session listed in the precheck output:
        1. Read the session card to get the &lt;purpose&gt; and &lt;time start="..."&gt;
        2. Choose a short descriptive name based on the purpose (2-4 words, underscores for spaces)
        3. Rename the directory: capture-YYYYMMDDTHHMM-Session_Name/
           The date part comes from the session's start time.

        Use cb move to rename:
        ```
        cb move box/inbox/capture-20260211T1951-f26ffa35 box/inbox/capture-20260211T1951-Whiteboard_Planning
        ```

        4. Set status="intake-complete" on the session card.

        COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Rename capture sessions

        Triggered-By: cb workflow
        Phase: rename
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>
  </step>
</workflow>
